@anon.3c5d4856225436a016f648d8ca8332b3.3159 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [878 x i8] }> <{ [878 x i8] c"# `trace_macros`\0A\0AThe tracking issue for this feature is [#29598].\0A\0A[#29598]: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/29598\0A\0A------------------------\0A\0AWith `trace_macros` you can trace the expansion of macros in your code.\0A\0A## Examples\0A\0A```rust\0A#![feature(trace_macros)]\0A\0Afn main() {\0A    trace_macros!(true);\0A    println!(\22Hello, Rust!\22);\0A    trace_macros!(false);\0A}\0A```\0A\0AThe `cargo build` output:\0A\0A```txt\0Anote: trace_macro\0A --> src/main.rs:5:5\0A  |\0A5 |     println!(\22Hello, Rust!\22);\0A  |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\0A  |\0A  = note: expanding `println! { \22Hello, Rust!\22 }`\0A  = note: to `print ! ( concat ! ( \22Hello, Rust!\22 , \22\\n\22 ) )`\0A  = note: expanding `print! { concat ! ( \22Hello, Rust!\22 , \22\\n\22 ) }`\0A  = note: to `$crate :: io :: _print ( format_args ! ( concat ! ( \22Hello, Rust!\22 , \22\\n\22 ) )\0A          )`\0A\0A    Finished dev [unoptimized + debuginfo] target(s) in 0.60 secs\0A```\0A" }>, align 1
